1
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:54,971
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

2
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:00,226
Can you trust me?

3
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:05,482
No matter what I do or say?

4
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:10,320
You don't have to answer me right now.

5
00:01:11,237 --> 00:01:12,072
But…

6
00:01:15,033 --> 00:01:15,992
for now…

7
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:19,120
I just want you to trust me.

8
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:26,878
Lee Ga-kyung.

9
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:28,713
Yes?

10
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:33,426
I mean…

11
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:35,512
I wasn't answering you.

12
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:37,347
Lee Ga-kyung suits you…

13
00:01:39,682 --> 00:01:41,726
much better than Keum Seo-hee.

14
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:48,024
Lee Ga-kyung.

15
00:01:52,237 --> 00:01:53,905
May I call you that?

16
00:01:57,408 --> 00:01:59,160
I do want an answer to that now.

17
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:14,300
Yes…

18
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:20,682
Interpreter Kim Tae-ung.

19
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:47,500
The inspector general
invited you to dinner at his residence?

20
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:49,210
That's right.

21
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:51,504
So-ran.

22
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:55,049
I really don't think
it's a good idea to go.

23
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:58,303
There's no way he'd invite us over
just for a pleasant evening.

24
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:00,638
Exactly.

25
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:03,558
The inspector general seemed
smarter than that.

26
00:03:03,641 --> 00:03:05,935
Does he think you'll come running
just because he asked?

27
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:08,021
We weren't born yesterday.

28
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:14,194
Are you thinking of going?

29
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:15,695
You're not, right?

30
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:19,449
You can't.

31
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:21,034
This has to be a trap.

32
00:03:21,117 --> 00:03:24,913
He already knows the Gugukdan
set off the bomb at the banquet.

33
00:03:24,996 --> 00:03:27,332
Wouldn't it look more suspicious
if we didn't go?

34
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:29,500
So-ran.

35
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:33,463
We can't even get a knife
past security at the residence.

36
00:03:33,546 --> 00:03:35,924
I'll come up with some kind of excuse.

37
00:03:36,007 --> 00:03:37,759
Let's not take any chances this time.

38
00:03:37,842 --> 00:03:39,427
Let's wait for the right time--

39
00:03:39,510 --> 00:03:41,679
There may never be a right time.

40
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:44,641
Sato's already closing in on us.

41
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:47,143
We'll have to face it sooner or later,

42
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,229
and we're really running out of time.

43
00:03:52,148 --> 00:03:54,692
Still, it's too dangerous
without any weapons.

44
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:56,736
Then I'll break a glass and use that.

45
00:03:57,362 --> 00:03:59,822
So-ran, we'll be in his house.

46
00:03:59,906 --> 00:04:01,658
I can't risk losing you there.

47
00:04:21,177 --> 00:04:22,136
In that case,

48
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:24,055
you should go.

49
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:27,976
But…

50
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:30,895
I have an idea.

51
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:36,192
<i>Send a bomb to the residence</i>
<i>through the pneumatic tube?</i>

52
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:37,235
Yes.

53
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:40,863
Do you all remember
this pneumatic tube thing?

54
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:46,869
The pneumatic tube system connects the
Government-General and Keijo Post Office.

55
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:50,748
It also links the Government-General
with both the governor-general's residence

56
00:04:50,832 --> 00:04:53,042
and the inspector general's residence.

57
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:56,045
The pneumatic tube carriers,
canisters that travel through the tubes,

58
00:04:56,129 --> 00:05:00,216
are about this big,
more than big enough to fit a bomb.

59
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,510
And we've got two bombs

60
00:05:02,593 --> 00:05:04,595
right here, in the ladies' room.

61
00:05:04,679 --> 00:05:07,140
It's right next
to the pneumatic tube room.

62
00:05:07,724 --> 00:05:10,226
The carriers take
just two and a half minutes

63
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:12,353
to reach the residences
from the Government-General.

64
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:15,064
I've seen the technical documents
and interpreted for them.

65
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:17,025
Trust me, it takes two and a half minutes.

66
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:19,277
Two and a half minutes.

67
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:22,363
So we could get a bomb
into both residences

68
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:25,575
in just two and a half minutes,
past all that security?

69
00:05:25,658 --> 00:05:27,618
The bombs are already
in the Government-General.

70
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:29,746
The governor-general hasn't left
his residence.

71
00:05:29,829 --> 00:05:33,374
This is our chance
to take out both men in one strike.

72
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,043
But you'll be in there too.

73
00:05:36,461 --> 00:05:37,545
Can you escape in time?

74
00:05:37,628 --> 00:05:40,048
I'll keep Sato in the study
where the pneumatic tube is,

75
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:41,132
then slip away.

76
00:05:41,215 --> 00:05:42,967
We have no more time to waste.

77
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:45,053
We need to do whatever we can.

78
00:05:45,803 --> 00:05:46,804
Ms. Ga-kyung.

79
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:47,847
I mean,

80
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:49,474
- Ms. Seo-hee.
- Yes.

81
00:05:49,557 --> 00:05:51,976
Anything else we should know
about the pneumatic tube system?

82
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:55,813
Before sending a carrier,
the staff call the residence first

83
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:57,231
<i>to let them know it's on its way.</i>

84
00:05:57,315 --> 00:05:58,816
A pneumatic tube carrier is coming

85
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,735
from the inspector general
to the governor-general,

86
00:06:00,818 --> 00:06:01,694
so please stand by.

87
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:07,784
<i>Two and a half minutes later,</i>
<i>it arrives at the residence.</i>

88
00:06:15,083 --> 00:06:18,378
<i>The residence staff hand it over to</i>
<i>the governor-general or inspector general.</i>

89
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:23,132
Factoring in the time
it'll take to reach the recipient,

90
00:06:23,216 --> 00:06:25,718
we'd need a bomb with a four-minute timer.

91
00:06:29,138 --> 00:06:29,972
Yes?

92
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:34,685
<i>We need to send the carriers to</i>
<i>both residences almost at the same time.</i>

93
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:42,151
<i>There's a chance</i>
<i>that one of them could open the carrier</i>

94
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:44,362
<i>before the four minutes are up.</i>

95
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:54,747
So we'll have to modify the bombs
to explode the moment

96
00:06:55,456 --> 00:06:56,874
the carriers are opened.

97
00:07:00,962 --> 00:07:03,297
Is there any way I could
get into the Government-General?

98
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:07,135
Security must be
extremely tight right now.

99
00:07:09,387 --> 00:07:12,849
Normally, the customer is supposed
to pick it up on the first floor.

100
00:07:12,932 --> 00:07:15,101
But "Toilet" makes me bring it inside.

101
00:07:15,184 --> 00:07:16,060
And that's every day.

102
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:18,312
There's a way.

103
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:24,152
I know someone
who really loves <i>naengmyeon.</i>

104
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:33,119
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

105
00:07:33,202 --> 00:07:35,496
EPISODE 12

106
00:07:48,384 --> 00:07:50,052
<i>Please make sure Sato Hideo,</i>

107
00:07:50,136 --> 00:07:51,846
the bastard who killed Songjeon,

108
00:07:51,929 --> 00:07:54,056
is in the study
with the inspector general.

109
00:07:54,682 --> 00:07:58,019
Our targets are the governor-general
and inspector general.

110
00:07:58,102 --> 00:07:59,937
Let's focus on our targets for now

111
00:08:00,021 --> 00:08:01,397
and leave the rest to fate.

112
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,358
Seo-hee.

113
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:06,944
You and Se-hwan

114
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:10,239
need to leave the Government-General
the moment you send the bombs.

115
00:08:11,115 --> 00:08:12,867
Lay low somewhere safe for a while.

116
00:08:13,701 --> 00:08:15,870
We'll move again when things settle down.

117
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:20,625
I guess tomorrow will be my last day

118
00:08:21,375 --> 00:08:22,960
working at the Government-General.

119
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:28,799
<i>He can't go to the residence today.</i>

120
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:31,302
<i>But he can't stay here either.</i>

121
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:33,804
<i>Then…</i>

122
00:08:34,472 --> 00:08:38,476
<i>this might be</i>
<i>the last time I ever see him.</i>

123
00:08:43,731 --> 00:08:45,149
Do you have a headache?

124
00:08:47,151 --> 00:08:48,027
No.

125
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:50,863
Your face says

126
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:53,241
you're having a rough day.

127
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:03,834
I feel like…

128
00:09:05,711 --> 00:09:07,880
English is starting
to stress me out today.

129
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:10,174
So,

130
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:12,176
I'm going to head out first.

131
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:13,135
What?

132
00:09:13,844 --> 00:09:14,804
You scared me.

133
00:09:15,304 --> 00:09:16,138
What is it?

134
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:19,225
Well…

135
00:09:19,934 --> 00:09:21,435
Are you leaving for the day?

136
00:09:22,019 --> 00:09:25,356
Are you heading to the residence, then?

137
00:09:25,439 --> 00:09:27,900
No, I'm on my way to see Mr. Kim.

138
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:31,904
Why are you meeting him?

139
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:33,281
What do you mean, why?

140
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:34,991
I need to talk to him about Gyodang-ri.

141
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:41,122
I was going to arrange a meeting with him
to discuss what happened yesterday.

142
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:42,248
When I got home,

143
00:09:42,331 --> 00:09:44,333
he'd already invited me to dinner today.

144
00:09:47,378 --> 00:09:50,131
I guess you'll be getting home late, then.

145
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:51,591
What a relief.

146
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:54,510
Sorry? What was that?

147
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:56,721
It's nothing.

148
00:09:59,223 --> 00:10:02,602
I know we've got a lot of work to do.
Sorry for taking off early.

149
00:10:04,437 --> 00:10:06,272
You should call it a day early.

150
00:10:06,355 --> 00:10:08,608
We can finish the rest together tomorrow.

151
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:14,280
All right, I'm off.

152
00:10:16,490 --> 00:10:17,366
Kim Tae-ung!

153
00:10:18,242 --> 00:10:19,285
What?

154
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:23,873
Mr. Kim.

155
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:30,588
You're just going to call me
by my name now?

156
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:33,049
Then I'll call you by your name too.

157
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:35,635
Lee Ga-kyung.

158
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:41,974
What is it?

159
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:45,311
Do you have something to say to me?

160
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:52,902
Take care.

161
00:10:53,903 --> 00:10:56,072
I'll see you when you get back.

162
00:10:58,115 --> 00:10:58,991
Thanks.

163
00:10:59,909 --> 00:11:01,619
I'll see you tomorrow, then.

164
00:11:03,954 --> 00:11:06,332
Oh, right.

165
00:11:06,415 --> 00:11:09,502
I've got a little sister.
Her name is Hanako.

166
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:11,587
Your little sister?

167
00:11:11,671 --> 00:11:15,508
Yes, you met her briefly
at Gyeongseong Station.

168
00:11:16,425 --> 00:11:19,220
It was the day someone stole my wallet.

169
00:11:20,971 --> 00:11:22,264
Hey, hold on.

170
00:11:25,184 --> 00:11:26,894
You mean that girl from…

171
00:11:27,687 --> 00:11:28,521
Yes.

172
00:11:29,188 --> 00:11:31,440
She's my Joseon mother's
biological daughter.

173
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:33,484
Hanako…

174
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:37,947
can't walk either.

175
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:43,411
I'm sorry. I was so insensitive back then.

176
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:44,662
No, it's okay.

177
00:11:48,165 --> 00:11:49,166
Maybe next time…

178
00:11:51,419 --> 00:11:52,670
we could all get together.

179
00:11:54,463 --> 00:11:57,675
I feel bad that Hanako's
stuck at home all the time.

180
00:11:57,758 --> 00:11:58,759
And somehow,

181
00:12:00,594 --> 00:12:02,012
you two have something in common.

182
00:12:04,014 --> 00:12:06,726
You should meet her sometime.

183
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:13,441
I'm waiting for your answer,

184
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:15,443
Ms. Lee Ga-kyung.

185
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:18,696
Sure.

186
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:25,745
I'm meeting him at Myeongwolgwan,
right around the corner.

187
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:28,038
I'm going to be late. See you tomorrow.

188
00:12:36,797 --> 00:12:38,257
He's gone.

189
00:12:44,096 --> 00:12:45,806
Will there be a next time?

190
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:50,853
You're all set.

191
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:19,131
So-ran.

192
00:13:23,677 --> 00:13:26,096
There's only one thing
you need to think about.

193
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:28,641
Your safety.

194
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:32,895
No matter what happens tonight,

195
00:13:32,978 --> 00:13:35,564
you're coming back to this house
safe and sound.

196
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:40,319
Shall we go?

197
00:13:50,329 --> 00:13:54,500
The guests are coming over
for dinner with Father.

198
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:57,878
So why are you cleaning the study?

199
00:13:58,504 --> 00:14:01,841
Because the guests
might want to look around the study.

200
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:03,217
The study?

201
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,219
What's there to see in the study?

202
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:07,805
There's nothing but books.

203
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:11,767
They might want to smoke in here.

204
00:14:11,851 --> 00:14:12,685
Smoke?

205
00:14:14,603 --> 00:14:18,858
Hideo can't handle
being around so much cigarette smoke.

206
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,652
So, who's coming over?

207
00:14:22,486 --> 00:14:25,573
Goodness, you're asking
a lot of questions today.

208
00:14:25,656 --> 00:14:27,533
I have no idea either.

209
00:14:27,616 --> 00:14:30,286
Things are chaotic now.
Why are we having guests over?

210
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:32,705
And he told me at the last minute.

211
00:14:32,788 --> 00:14:34,915
I said, who's coming over?

212
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:36,959
Your guess is as good as mine.

213
00:14:37,042 --> 00:14:37,960
What did you say?

214
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:41,255
Speak in a language I can understand.

215
00:14:41,338 --> 00:14:43,173
Yanagi!

216
00:14:44,341 --> 00:14:45,718
Yanagi!

217
00:14:47,261 --> 00:14:48,637
Yanagi!

218
00:14:53,058 --> 00:14:56,020
Our comrades are putting their lives
on the line again today.

219
00:14:57,396 --> 00:14:59,189
And here I am, going off to Hwawol

220
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:01,901
to enjoy some Japanese food
just because my dad insists.

221
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:05,195
What a joke.

222
00:15:06,405 --> 00:15:07,615
I'm absolutely pathetic.

223
00:15:09,533 --> 00:15:12,494
Not every member of our group
takes part in every operation.

224
00:15:12,578 --> 00:15:14,204
We need to consider our next move.

225
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:15,497
Don't be so hard on yourself.

226
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:17,374
Will I ever get the chance

227
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:20,002
to hold a gun or a knife

228
00:15:20,085 --> 00:15:21,921
instead of a purse or a hand mirror?

229
00:15:23,380 --> 00:15:25,424
Guns and knives aren't the only weapons.

230
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:28,135
What's supposed to be my weapon?

231
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:32,222
That my father's the worst
pro-Japanese traitor in Joseon?

232
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:42,983
I hear she's leaving for Shanghai
after this operation.

233
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:47,780
Shanghai…

234
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:52,493
I'm jealous.

235
00:16:05,422 --> 00:16:06,340
Myung-nam.

236
00:16:08,008 --> 00:16:11,178
You're supposed to be
a quiet and demure young lady.

237
00:16:11,261 --> 00:16:12,721
Don't forget to act like one.

238
00:16:13,430 --> 00:16:15,057
What are you talking about?

239
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:16,058
Aren't you getting in?

240
00:16:17,226 --> 00:16:20,104
Especially around your fiancé,
keep your voice down

241
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:21,647
and your temper in check.

242
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:22,731
Do you understand?

243
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:24,358
What? My fiancé?

244
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:29,655
I must say, your future father-in-law
has quite a sense of humor.

245
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:33,701
Anyway, go there
and make sure you smile a lot today.

246
00:16:33,784 --> 00:16:34,618
All right.

247
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:36,245
Young-bok, get moving.

248
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:41,875
What's going on?

249
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:43,961
My father and the inspector general

250
00:16:44,044 --> 00:16:47,214
plotted to trick me
into meeting Sato Hideo?

251
00:16:47,297 --> 00:16:48,132
Yes.

252
00:16:48,632 --> 00:16:49,466
That's great.

253
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:51,051
What's great about that?

254
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:52,886
No way. I'm not going.

255
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:56,473
Hold on.

256
00:16:58,267 --> 00:17:00,477
So Sato Hideo won't be at his residence.

257
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:02,479
He's coming to Hwawol instead?

258
00:17:05,816 --> 00:17:06,817
Let's take a gun with us.

259
00:17:17,077 --> 00:17:18,871
Welcome, Mr. Yoo.

260
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:20,998
Mrs. Yoo.

261
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:23,042
How have you been?

262
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:25,586
Thanks for coming on such short notice.

263
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:29,256
I've been meaning
to have you two over to my residence.

264
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:31,175
I'm sorry it took so long.

265
00:17:31,759 --> 00:17:34,344
Not at all.
We're grateful for your kind invitation.

266
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:39,600
This is my daughter, Hanako.

267
00:17:40,350 --> 00:17:41,185
Hanako.

268
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:01,121
It's lovely to meet you, Miss Hanako.

269
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:03,248
Hello.

270
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:06,335
What a lovely young lady.

271
00:18:09,129 --> 00:18:09,963
Yanagi.

272
00:18:14,218 --> 00:18:16,845
We'll get you to your room now.

273
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:20,974
We have company, so don't wander around.

274
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:26,396
Please, right this way.

275
00:18:27,815 --> 00:18:29,733
Mr. Hideo doesn't seem to be here.

276
00:18:32,569 --> 00:18:35,531
Hideo had a prior engagement,
so he couldn't make it today.

277
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:58,512
This way, please.

278
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:10,691
Inspector General.

279
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:16,947
Even from the foyer, the residence
is as beautiful as I'd heard.

280
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:19,908
Would you mind showing us
around the place before dinner?

281
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:23,370
That's a great idea.

282
00:19:24,496 --> 00:19:25,414
But

283
00:19:25,497 --> 00:19:28,333
I've prepared a rather special drink
for this occasion.

284
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:29,626
Let's start with dinner.

285
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:32,462
It's a real honor. In fact…

286
00:19:34,882 --> 00:19:38,594
though I'm just a humble reporter,
I happen to be quite an avid reader.

287
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:41,054
I heard you had
quite a collection of books.

288
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:45,142
I was so curious about your study
that I could hardly sleep last night.

289
00:19:47,436 --> 00:19:48,770
Didn't I just tell you?

290
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:50,981
Sorry?

291
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:53,233
I said I had something prepared.

292
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:57,362
Very well.

293
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:02,868
I've been so looking forward
to having dinner with you both.

294
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:06,330
I'd hate to see the food get cold.

295
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:09,791
So let's enjoy dinner first
and look around the residence afterward.

296
00:20:20,928 --> 00:20:23,347
OUT OF ORDER

297
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:43,784
You're all set.

298
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:45,577
Thank you very much.

299
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:53,043
Hey, <i>yobo.</i>

300
00:20:57,256 --> 00:21:00,759
Are you from Gyeongdo Noodle House?
I've never seen you before.

301
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:03,303
Our regular deliveryman

302
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:05,681
was hit by a car and got hurt.

303
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:09,268
Gyeongdo Noodle House? That's for
Mr. Mitarai in the pneumatic tube room.

304
00:21:09,893 --> 00:21:10,727
Let him in.

305
00:21:11,603 --> 00:21:12,604
Thank you.

306
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:20,237
LADIES' ROOM

307
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:22,781
OUT OF ORDER

308
00:21:28,745 --> 00:21:32,374
I was wondering what kind of <i>naengmyeon</i>
he kept ordering.

309
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:33,625
Gyeongdo Noodle House?

310
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:36,962
Why do these Japanese guys
have such weird taste buds?

311
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:39,298
Right? I'm not a fan of this place either.

312
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:41,675
Who else likes Gyeongdo Noodle House?

313
00:21:41,758 --> 00:21:42,801
There's someone.

314
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:45,429
A Japanese guy with bad taste in food.

315
00:21:46,763 --> 00:21:51,101
He was always going on and on about
Gyeongdo Noodle House's <i>naengmyeon.</i>

316
00:21:51,643 --> 00:21:55,147
He even told me to get a job there
so he could get a discount.

317
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:57,107
Unbelievable.

318
00:21:57,899 --> 00:21:59,901
When it comes to <i>naengmyeon, </i>nothing beats

319
00:21:59,985 --> 00:22:01,611
- Hanseong Cold…
- Hanseong Cold Noodles.

320
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:07,075
Finally, someone with good taste.

321
00:22:21,715 --> 00:22:23,967
I hope you enjoy the food.

322
00:22:25,052 --> 00:22:26,011
You're too kind.

323
00:22:26,511 --> 00:22:29,598
People like us don't get to visit
a place like this every day.

324
00:22:30,265 --> 00:22:32,726
Truth be told,
I don't host dinners very often.

325
00:22:32,809 --> 00:22:35,729
My wife was the one
who normally arranged these gatherings.

326
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:38,857
I heard your wife passed away last year.

327
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:40,233
Accept my belated condolences.

328
00:22:40,317 --> 00:22:41,234
I appreciate that.

329
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:43,487
She was frail for most of her life.

330
00:22:45,197 --> 00:22:46,698
Hanako's from my previous marriage.

331
00:22:48,075 --> 00:22:51,286
I had a Joseon wife,
but she died in childbirth.

332
00:22:53,538 --> 00:22:55,165
Anyway, Mr. Yoo.

333
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:57,626
How are things going for you in Joseon?

334
00:22:57,709 --> 00:23:00,295
I hear you've been traveling
all over Joseon for your reporting.

335
00:23:01,088 --> 00:23:03,382
I've been staying in Gyeongseong
for the most part lately.

336
00:23:04,633 --> 00:23:05,509
I see.

337
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:10,680
Back when I was a soldier,
I traveled all over Joseon myself.

338
00:23:11,515 --> 00:23:12,474
Hamgyong-do,

339
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:15,394
Gangwon-do, Jeolla-do, and Gyeongsang-do.

340
00:23:15,894 --> 00:23:18,897
It was fun trying
the specialties of each region.

341
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:24,319
Seeing all these local specialties
from Joseon in one place makes me feel…

342
00:23:29,658 --> 00:23:31,576
What's that word
in the Joseon language again?

343
00:23:33,328 --> 00:23:34,496
Nostalgic.

344
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:37,999
It makes me feel nostalgic.

345
00:23:42,254 --> 00:23:44,047
These bamboo shoots are from Jeolla-do.

346
00:23:44,131 --> 00:23:45,257
They're in season right now.

347
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:46,842
Do you like bamboo shoots, Mrs. Yoo?

348
00:23:48,009 --> 00:23:48,844
Yes.

349
00:23:48,927 --> 00:23:51,304
I heard bamboo shoots are common
in Chinese cuisine.

350
00:23:52,180 --> 00:23:53,557
Where is your hometown?

351
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:55,642
I'm from Shanghai.

352
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:57,144
Shanghai.

353
00:23:57,227 --> 00:23:58,437
It's a fine city.

354
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:03,400
You're probably still not very familiar
with Joseon cuisine, are you?

355
00:24:04,025 --> 00:24:06,611
She's not used to Joseon food yet.

356
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:07,988
I can imagine.

357
00:24:08,071 --> 00:24:10,699
Then this should be
quite an experience for you.

358
00:24:11,408 --> 00:24:13,535
Joseon has plenty of interesting dishes.

359
00:24:17,122 --> 00:24:18,206
I'll give you an example.

360
00:24:19,207 --> 00:24:21,376
Do you know
a dish called <i>chutang </i>tofu soup?

361
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:25,922
It's also called <i>chutang,</i>

362
00:24:26,423 --> 00:24:28,133
or <i>chueo </i>tofu<i>.</i>

363
00:24:29,634 --> 00:24:31,636
It's a dish made by boiling loaches.

364
00:24:32,846 --> 00:24:35,432
The fascinating thing
about this dish is how it's made.

365
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:38,810
First, you put the loaches in cold water

366
00:24:38,894 --> 00:24:42,105
with the tofu,
then slowly turn up the heat.

367
00:24:44,649 --> 00:24:46,860
Do you know what the loaches do
when the water gets hot?

368
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:54,701
To avoid the boiling water,
they wriggle their way into the tofu.

369
00:24:56,495 --> 00:24:59,039
They believe they can hold out
inside the tofu.

370
00:24:59,122 --> 00:25:03,335
But once the water boils,
the tofu heats up too, doesn't it?

371
00:25:03,877 --> 00:25:07,547
So the loaches end up
being cooked inside the tofu.

372
00:25:09,132 --> 00:25:10,300
I have

373
00:25:10,383 --> 00:25:12,886
never quite understood those loaches.

374
00:25:14,596 --> 00:25:16,181
The water is boiling,

375
00:25:17,140 --> 00:25:20,435
so how could they think
they'd survive by hiding inside the tofu?

376
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:23,396
Do you get it, Mrs. Yoo?

377
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,902
Well, it does make for a delicacy.

378
00:25:28,985 --> 00:25:32,113
I suppose we don't really need to know
what the loaches think.

379
00:25:35,909 --> 00:25:37,327
This rice cake

380
00:25:37,869 --> 00:25:40,247
is made with rice
from a village in Gyeonggi-do.

381
00:25:40,747 --> 00:25:42,874
The place was famous for its fertile land.

382
00:25:44,292 --> 00:25:46,545
I believe it was called Kyeam-ri.

383
00:26:01,101 --> 00:26:03,436
It was a place
with vast stretches of farmland.

384
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:07,899
There was a bit of trouble there
a long time ago.

385
00:26:12,612 --> 00:26:15,282
I see. What about the wild spring greens--

386
00:26:15,365 --> 00:26:17,117
There was a man in that village.

387
00:26:18,285 --> 00:26:19,286
That man

388
00:26:19,786 --> 00:26:22,414
never revealed his comrades' names,
even until the very end.

389
00:26:22,998 --> 00:26:24,332
He wouldn't talk

390
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:27,877
even when we pointed a gun at his daughter

391
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:30,088
right in front of him.

392
00:26:36,428 --> 00:26:37,554
Shoot.

393
00:26:37,637 --> 00:26:38,805
No!

394
00:26:43,977 --> 00:26:47,439
He chose his convictions
over his own child.

395
00:26:48,064 --> 00:26:50,191
I have to admit, I was quite impressed.

396
00:27:00,410 --> 00:27:01,953
I almost forgot the wine.

397
00:27:02,621 --> 00:27:03,872
This one's from 1919.

398
00:27:04,539 --> 00:27:05,749
Thirteen years.

399
00:27:05,832 --> 00:27:07,208
It's aged quite a bit.

400
00:27:08,752 --> 00:27:10,337
A fine wine is best

401
00:27:11,254 --> 00:27:13,465
when you've let it age.

402
00:27:15,717 --> 00:27:16,676
But

403
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:18,595
what happened next
is even more interesting.

404
00:27:21,139 --> 00:27:25,018
Only after his daughter died did he
finally give up his comrades' names.

405
00:27:25,852 --> 00:27:27,395
Of course, it was too late.

406
00:27:28,688 --> 00:27:29,856
Why would he do that?

407
00:27:30,398 --> 00:27:33,193
He kept his mouth shut
while his daughter was alive,

408
00:27:33,276 --> 00:27:34,944
but finally spoke after she died.

409
00:27:35,987 --> 00:27:38,323
He's like those loaches, wouldn't you say?

410
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:46,331
He thought he could protect his daughter

411
00:27:46,873 --> 00:27:49,250
if he held out
and stayed true to his beliefs.

412
00:27:49,334 --> 00:27:50,502
But in the end,

413
00:27:51,378 --> 00:27:54,714
he failed to protect his daughter
or stay true to his beliefs.

414
00:27:56,383 --> 00:27:58,218
It's all so pointless, isn't it?

415
00:28:14,150 --> 00:28:16,695
So the carrier should reach Sato's study

416
00:28:16,778 --> 00:28:19,072
sometime between 6:30 p.m. and 6:40 p.m.

417
00:28:19,155 --> 00:28:20,031
Right.

418
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:24,744
I'll stall him and make sure
he's in the study until then.

419
00:28:26,121 --> 00:28:27,497
His wife

420
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:29,457
was there too.

421
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:31,918
Mrs. Yoo.

422
00:28:32,752 --> 00:28:34,963
How do you think
that woman went on living after that?

423
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:39,342
Sir, you have a phone call.

424
00:28:39,426 --> 00:28:40,844
There are two possibilities.

425
00:28:41,428 --> 00:28:42,387
She either

426
00:28:42,470 --> 00:28:44,723
kept her daughter in her heart
and lived quietly,

427
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:46,474
or…

428
00:28:48,226 --> 00:28:49,853
lived for the day she could get revenge.

429
00:28:58,611 --> 00:29:01,281
If she decided to get revenge,

430
00:29:01,364 --> 00:29:02,198
well,

431
00:29:03,366 --> 00:29:04,617
what do you think would happen?

432
00:29:05,368 --> 00:29:06,494
Inspector General.

433
00:29:13,001 --> 00:29:14,878
It's an old Chinese proverb.

434
00:29:16,171 --> 00:29:17,255
In the Joseon language,

435
00:29:18,256 --> 00:29:21,426
<i>cheonmanghoehoe, soibullu.</i>

436
00:29:21,509 --> 00:29:23,386
THOSE WHO DO WRONG
CAN'T ESCAPE HEAVEN'S WRATH

437
00:29:27,432 --> 00:29:30,310
Heaven's net may look
wide and full of holes,

438
00:29:31,561 --> 00:29:33,688
yet it lets nothing through.

439
00:29:38,318 --> 00:29:40,361
I see your Joseon language
has improved quite a bit.

440
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:41,321
Yes.

441
00:29:42,739 --> 00:29:44,574
It's a very wise saying.

442
00:29:44,657 --> 00:29:46,034
It certainly is.

443
00:29:47,285 --> 00:29:48,286
In other words,

444
00:29:49,537 --> 00:29:51,623
justice will prevail,

445
00:29:51,706 --> 00:29:54,834
so there's no need to take matters
into our own hands, is there?

446
00:29:55,835 --> 00:29:57,837
If you forget your place and get involved,

447
00:29:58,338 --> 00:30:02,008
you may end up getting caught
in Heaven's net.

448
00:30:06,930 --> 00:30:07,764
Come in.

449
00:30:11,559 --> 00:30:12,602
I'm sorry to interrupt.

450
00:30:12,685 --> 00:30:13,978
What is it?

451
00:30:14,062 --> 00:30:16,815
A pneumatic tube carrier has arrived
from the Government-General.

452
00:30:16,898 --> 00:30:18,274
Leave it there.

453
00:30:18,358 --> 00:30:19,651
Yes, sir.

454
00:30:29,410 --> 00:30:30,745
Would you mind opening it for me?

455
00:30:32,914 --> 00:30:34,624
I can't get this wine open.

456
00:30:42,382 --> 00:30:46,052
I'd hate to break it by opening it myself.

457
00:30:46,135 --> 00:30:47,720
Allow me to open the wine bottle.

458
00:30:48,346 --> 00:30:49,389
Very well, then.

459
00:31:04,821 --> 00:31:05,947
Can't you get it open?

460
00:31:07,699 --> 00:31:08,533
No, it's fine.

461
00:31:41,107 --> 00:31:41,941
There we go.

462
00:32:15,141 --> 00:32:16,809
I have one more little surprise

463
00:32:18,061 --> 00:32:19,771
for both of you.

464
00:32:24,776 --> 00:32:25,777
I think Keum Seo-hee

465
00:32:26,945 --> 00:32:28,029
is a spy.

466
00:32:32,116 --> 00:32:34,494
This means Keum Seo-hee

467
00:32:35,078 --> 00:32:35,912
is under arrest.

468
00:32:35,995 --> 00:32:36,829
COMPLETE

469
00:32:42,251 --> 00:32:44,045
There was a man named Keum Seok-jung.

470
00:32:45,004 --> 00:32:48,091
It was the foolish father from Kyeam-ri
that I just mentioned.

471
00:32:49,258 --> 00:32:51,678
He got caught recently
after trying to kill me.

472
00:32:53,596 --> 00:32:55,348
As it happens, his daughter's name

473
00:32:56,599 --> 00:32:57,892
was Keum Seo-hee.

474
00:32:59,310 --> 00:33:02,814
Do you want us to arrest
Keum Seo-hee tonight?

475
00:33:03,731 --> 00:33:04,899
But we don't have proof--

476
00:33:04,983 --> 00:33:07,026
The name Keum Seo-hee

477
00:33:07,694 --> 00:33:08,528
is proof.

478
00:33:10,029 --> 00:33:11,239
Keum Seo-hee.

479
00:33:12,991 --> 00:33:15,994
Keum Seok-jung's wife named her
after the daughter she'd lost.

480
00:33:17,286 --> 00:33:19,539
That means they have a special bond.

481
00:33:20,873 --> 00:33:23,042
If a woman who'd already lost a child

482
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:26,879
found another girl
with the same name in danger,

483
00:33:28,047 --> 00:33:30,008
could she possibly stay calm?

484
00:33:40,977 --> 00:33:43,271
When Interpreter Trainee Keum Seo-hee
leaves for the day,

485
00:33:43,354 --> 00:33:44,939
don't let her leave the building.

486
00:33:45,023 --> 00:33:45,857
Yes, sir.

487
00:34:17,180 --> 00:34:18,264
Hello.

488
00:34:18,347 --> 00:34:19,807
RECORDS ROOM

489
00:34:29,734 --> 00:34:30,693
How may I help you?

490
00:34:52,256 --> 00:34:55,676
<i>Keum Seo-hee must be closely connected</i>
<i>to Keum Seok-jung and his circle.</i>

491
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:58,679
<i>That's why I had Keum Seo-hee arrested</i>

492
00:34:58,763 --> 00:35:01,140
<i>and brought directly here.</i>

493
00:35:02,934 --> 00:35:05,686
We'll find out once we question her.

494
00:35:06,354 --> 00:35:07,688
She should be on her way here.

495
00:35:08,689 --> 00:35:09,857
She was your live-in maid.

496
00:35:10,483 --> 00:35:12,151
I guess she deceived you both.

497
00:35:12,235 --> 00:35:14,112
Wouldn't it be best
to confront her in person?

498
00:35:20,535 --> 00:35:22,328
MYEONGWOLGWAN

499
00:35:26,666 --> 00:35:28,334
Once we hear from the inspector general,

500
00:35:28,417 --> 00:35:30,253
- arrest him right away.
- Yes, sir.

501
00:35:32,797 --> 00:35:35,883
HWAWOL

502
00:35:54,402 --> 00:35:55,653
In hindsight,

503
00:35:55,736 --> 00:35:58,823
there were plenty of suspicious things
about her from day one.

504
00:35:59,490 --> 00:36:03,494
Most Joseon people would lower their heads
just passing the Government-General.

505
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:06,581
Yet she had the nerve to work there

506
00:36:07,373 --> 00:36:10,251
and come and go as if she owned the place.

507
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:13,504
And she certainly knew how to do her job.

508
00:36:13,588 --> 00:36:14,964
You saw her at the banquet.

509
00:36:16,549 --> 00:36:19,719
I bet she was sharp
when she served you as your maid.

510
00:36:20,428 --> 00:36:21,345
What was she like?

511
00:36:26,642 --> 00:36:29,395
I'm afraid
there's been a misunderstanding.

512
00:36:29,896 --> 00:36:30,813
Seo-hee is just--

513
00:36:30,897 --> 00:36:33,608
She had the nerve
to join the Government-General as a spy.

514
00:36:33,691 --> 00:36:35,359
She's quite a bold little thing.

515
00:36:36,569 --> 00:36:38,529
I have to admire her nerve.

516
00:36:38,613 --> 00:36:42,074
It's a shame she threw her life away
for such a foolish cause.

517
00:36:47,663 --> 00:36:49,540
Once we take her into custody,

518
00:36:49,624 --> 00:36:53,044
we'll have to search your home,
so I hope you'll understand.

519
00:36:53,628 --> 00:36:55,338
There's no need to be concerned.

520
00:36:55,421 --> 00:36:57,882
Neither of you is involved
in this matter, are you?

521
00:37:04,513 --> 00:37:05,431
Or am I wrong?

522
00:37:07,016 --> 00:37:08,309
Are you involved?

523
00:37:12,897 --> 00:37:15,066
The chief of police is here, sir.

524
00:37:25,117 --> 00:37:25,952
Let him in.

525
00:37:34,001 --> 00:37:34,919
Inspector General.

526
00:37:57,275 --> 00:37:58,150
How could this be?

527
00:38:24,760 --> 00:38:26,637
20 MINUTES AGO

528
00:38:26,721 --> 00:38:28,723
ENGLISH TRANSLATION UNIT

529
00:38:35,229 --> 00:38:36,439
So she's still here?

530
00:38:36,522 --> 00:38:37,523
Yes.

531
00:38:37,606 --> 00:38:39,442
She should be
in the Foreign Affairs Division.

532
00:38:39,525 --> 00:38:41,235
Why are we supposed to arrest her?

533
00:38:41,736 --> 00:38:43,279
I'm not really sure.

534
00:39:09,096 --> 00:39:10,806
There you are. Let's hurry.

535
00:39:10,890 --> 00:39:12,099
Okay.

536
00:39:14,268 --> 00:39:16,687
Your <i>naengmyeon </i>is here.

537
00:39:16,771 --> 00:39:17,813
Come in.

538
00:39:17,897 --> 00:39:18,731
Yes, sir!

539
00:39:26,322 --> 00:39:27,990
The bombs. I need to get the bombs out.

540
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:34,580
Hello there.

541
00:39:34,663 --> 00:39:35,539
Ms. Keum.

542
00:39:49,095 --> 00:39:50,513
That looked perfect.

543
00:39:50,596 --> 00:39:51,931
Why are you wiping it off?

544
00:39:52,014 --> 00:39:53,432
I don't like it.

545
00:40:10,783 --> 00:40:12,284
It looks perfect now!

546
00:40:12,368 --> 00:40:14,495
- It really does!
- No.

547
00:40:14,995 --> 00:40:17,706
Wearing lipstick is all about the heart.

548
00:40:18,290 --> 00:40:21,001
If your heart isn't right,

549
00:40:21,794 --> 00:40:24,088
then your lips are a lie.

550
00:40:25,798 --> 00:40:26,882
Is that so?

551
00:40:39,937 --> 00:40:40,980
Hey, you.

552
00:40:41,063 --> 00:40:42,523
I've never seen you before.

553
00:40:43,065 --> 00:40:44,233
Are you the new <i>yobo?</i>

554
00:40:44,942 --> 00:40:45,776
Sorry?

555
00:40:45,860 --> 00:40:46,694
"Sorry?"

556
00:40:48,362 --> 00:40:49,822
You ignorant fool.

557
00:40:49,905 --> 00:40:52,116
You can't even understand basic Japanese.

558
00:40:52,783 --> 00:40:54,952
You <i>Josenjings </i>are hopeless.

559
00:40:55,035 --> 00:40:58,706
No matter how much we Japanese teach you,
you're still useless.

560
00:40:58,789 --> 00:41:00,291
You imbecile.

561
00:41:00,374 --> 00:41:01,292
Do you understand?

562
00:41:07,965 --> 00:41:11,343
You don't even know what I'm saying.
You just stand there smiling.

563
00:41:11,427 --> 00:41:12,678
What a pathetic moron.

564
00:41:13,345 --> 00:41:14,346
Get out of here!

565
00:41:14,847 --> 00:41:16,182
Come back when I call you.

566
00:41:17,183 --> 00:41:18,017
Yes, sir.

567
00:41:18,767 --> 00:41:20,227
What a complete moron.

568
00:41:22,688 --> 00:41:23,647
This is so good!

569
00:41:26,942 --> 00:41:28,068
Mr. Sato.

570
00:41:28,152 --> 00:41:29,737
What brings you back?

571
00:41:30,613 --> 00:41:32,656
I'd like to call someone from the staff.

572
00:41:33,616 --> 00:41:35,159
Could you pass this along for me?

573
00:41:35,242 --> 00:41:37,203
I'm running late for dinner.

574
00:41:37,286 --> 00:41:38,662
Sure, I'll take it.

575
00:41:40,331 --> 00:41:41,999
Who should I deliver it to?

576
00:41:43,292 --> 00:41:45,377
No, actually, I'll deliver it myself.

577
00:41:45,461 --> 00:41:46,295
Yes, sir.

578
00:41:48,464 --> 00:41:50,090
Keum Seo-hee isn't in there!

579
00:41:50,174 --> 00:41:51,634
Maybe she caught on and ran away.

580
00:41:51,717 --> 00:41:52,718
Find her! Now!

581
00:41:52,801 --> 00:41:53,719
Yes, sir!

582
00:41:53,802 --> 00:41:56,096
We've made sure
she can't leave the building.

583
00:42:06,982 --> 00:42:07,983
Oh, look.

584
00:42:08,692 --> 00:42:10,444
We're wearing similar outfits.

585
00:42:11,237 --> 00:42:14,782
Mine is from Ginza Boutique.

586
00:42:14,865 --> 00:42:16,325
Where did you get yours?

587
00:42:18,244 --> 00:42:20,412
That's not important right now.

588
00:42:24,917 --> 00:42:26,544
Yes, you're right!

589
00:42:27,127 --> 00:42:29,046
Clothes are important.

590
00:42:29,129 --> 00:42:30,464
Where did you get yours?

591
00:42:30,548 --> 00:42:33,050
You didn't have it made in Jongno,
did you?

592
00:42:33,133 --> 00:42:36,762
Clothes made by <i>Josenjings</i>
look a little cheap to me.

593
00:42:36,845 --> 00:42:38,430
Oh, no offense.

594
00:42:39,557 --> 00:42:40,391
No, it's fine.

595
00:42:43,852 --> 00:42:45,646
Listen, Ms. Yamada.

596
00:42:47,565 --> 00:42:50,693
You know, about Interpreter Sato.

597
00:42:51,318 --> 00:42:53,612
Yes? What about him?

598
00:42:54,572 --> 00:42:56,156
About his engagement…

599
00:42:56,699 --> 00:42:57,825
The truth is…

600
00:42:59,326 --> 00:43:01,370
it's an arranged marriage without love.

601
00:43:04,707 --> 00:43:05,624
Because…

602
00:43:07,668 --> 00:43:09,962
deep in his heart,

603
00:43:10,796 --> 00:43:11,672
he's always loved

604
00:43:12,339 --> 00:43:13,257
you, Ms. Yamada.

605
00:43:14,633 --> 00:43:15,467
Oh my.

606
00:43:17,428 --> 00:43:18,262
Actually,

607
00:43:18,887 --> 00:43:21,724
Mr. Sato is in the Records Room
at the moment.

608
00:43:21,807 --> 00:43:22,766
Records Room?

609
00:43:22,850 --> 00:43:25,269
Yes, because of work.

610
00:43:25,352 --> 00:43:26,812
He's there alone.

611
00:43:27,938 --> 00:43:28,814
What if

612
00:43:28,897 --> 00:43:32,109
you went to the Records Room right now?

613
00:43:32,693 --> 00:43:33,777
You might,

614
00:43:33,861 --> 00:43:35,279
by pure coincidence…

615
00:43:35,362 --> 00:43:37,323
- Run into each other.
- Yes, exactly!

616
00:43:37,406 --> 00:43:38,490
Do you see what I mean?

617
00:43:38,574 --> 00:43:42,369
Romance in popular fiction
always starts in a library.

618
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:45,914
Imagine you and Mr. Sato alone
in the Records Room.

619
00:43:45,998 --> 00:43:48,751
Then a pile of books
comes tumbling off the shelves.

620
00:43:50,628 --> 00:43:52,004
My goodness!

621
00:43:52,087 --> 00:43:54,757
That's all I'll say!

622
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:56,592
What do I do?

623
00:43:56,675 --> 00:43:58,093
Go on, hurry!

624
00:43:59,553 --> 00:44:01,013
Wait, what do I do?

625
00:44:01,597 --> 00:44:02,514
It's flawless!

626
00:44:02,598 --> 00:44:03,807
Come on, off you go.

627
00:44:03,891 --> 00:44:04,850
Do my lips look okay?

628
00:44:04,933 --> 00:44:06,644
They look fine. Now go see him.

629
00:44:16,445 --> 00:44:19,990
OUT OF ORDER

630
00:44:26,955 --> 00:44:30,876
When the time comes,
go in first and send it.

631
00:44:31,752 --> 00:44:33,212
I need to take care of something.

632
00:44:34,088 --> 00:44:35,172
Okay.

633
00:44:41,762 --> 00:44:42,930
Hello.

634
00:44:44,723 --> 00:44:45,849
YAMADA HANAKO

635
00:44:47,267 --> 00:44:49,353
I'm here to find some records.

636
00:44:49,436 --> 00:44:50,688
Of course.

637
00:44:50,771 --> 00:44:52,606
KEUM SEO-HEE

638
00:45:18,716 --> 00:45:19,842
When the books

639
00:45:20,551 --> 00:45:23,512
come tumbling down…

640
00:45:24,221 --> 00:45:25,055
Mr. Sato

641
00:45:26,056 --> 00:45:28,058
would protect me like this, wouldn't he?

642
00:45:29,017 --> 00:45:30,185
And then…

643
00:45:34,690 --> 00:45:35,983
What do I do?

644
00:45:38,193 --> 00:45:41,697
It's embarrassing
with the lights this bright.

645
00:45:47,911 --> 00:45:49,830
Come on, please come this way.

646
00:46:04,178 --> 00:46:05,387
Can I help you?

647
00:46:19,234 --> 00:46:20,194
Mr. Hideo?

648
00:46:37,753 --> 00:46:39,171
I'm so sorry.

649
00:46:55,771 --> 00:46:57,689
Send this
to the inspector general's residence.

650
00:46:57,773 --> 00:46:58,690
Yes, sir.

651
00:47:07,324 --> 00:47:10,744
Operator, put me through
to the inspector general's residence.

652
00:47:16,625 --> 00:47:17,459
Hello?

653
00:47:17,543 --> 00:47:20,337
This is the Government-General's
pneumatic tube room.

654
00:47:20,420 --> 00:47:22,923
We're sending a pneumatic tube carrier
to the residence.

655
00:47:23,006 --> 00:47:24,299
Understood.

656
00:47:35,227 --> 00:47:36,395
INSPECTOR GENERAL

657
00:47:53,495 --> 00:47:54,413
Se-hwan.

658
00:47:55,539 --> 00:47:57,249
Please make it out in one piece.

659
00:48:04,131 --> 00:48:05,257
That delivery boy went in a while ago.

660
00:48:05,757 --> 00:48:07,843
What's taking him so long?

661
00:48:13,849 --> 00:48:15,601
<i>Yobo! </i>Come collect the bowl!

662
00:48:25,027 --> 00:48:27,154
Why are you so slow?

663
00:48:27,237 --> 00:48:28,655
Get the bowl out of here!

664
00:48:28,739 --> 00:48:31,617
<i>Josenjings </i>are always so slow.

665
00:49:06,318 --> 00:49:07,235
It's me.

666
00:49:21,917 --> 00:49:23,168
- Hello, Mr. Sato.
- Hello.

667
00:49:24,336 --> 00:49:26,380
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

668
00:49:26,463 --> 00:49:28,632
You're the guard posted
at the side gate, aren't you?

669
00:49:29,257 --> 00:49:30,384
Is something going on?

670
00:49:30,467 --> 00:49:31,885
You were looking for someone.

671
00:49:32,886 --> 00:49:35,472
The <i>naengmyeon </i>delivery boy
went to the pneumatic tube room

672
00:49:35,555 --> 00:49:37,349
and hasn't come out,
so I'm looking for him.

673
00:49:38,058 --> 00:49:40,185
I wanted to make sure everything was okay.

674
00:49:40,268 --> 00:49:42,562
Then I'll go see what's going on.

675
00:49:42,646 --> 00:49:44,147
You shouldn't leave your post.

676
00:49:44,231 --> 00:49:46,108
- But--
- It's all right.

677
00:49:46,191 --> 00:49:49,987
I just remembered I needed to go
to the pneumatic tube room anyway.

678
00:49:50,070 --> 00:49:51,446
I'll check on him while I'm there.

679
00:49:51,530 --> 00:49:53,031
Thank you very much, Mr. Sato.

680
00:50:01,415 --> 00:50:03,583
Never let Keum Seo-hee leave the building.

681
00:50:03,667 --> 00:50:05,210
Search every inch of the building!

682
00:50:05,293 --> 00:50:07,838
We have to find her
before the chief of police gets here!

683
00:50:07,921 --> 00:50:08,922
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

684
00:50:10,674 --> 00:50:12,300
Just wait until I catch you.

685
00:50:12,884 --> 00:50:14,761
You sneaky little rat.

686
00:50:22,811 --> 00:50:23,854
What's taking him so long?

687
00:50:24,855 --> 00:50:26,940
He doesn't seem like the type to be late.

688
00:50:29,609 --> 00:50:30,610
Something feels off.

689
00:50:36,241 --> 00:50:37,659
Take me to the Government-General.

690
00:50:37,743 --> 00:50:39,411
Something must be going on there.

691
00:50:49,087 --> 00:50:50,130
We're all set.

692
00:50:55,761 --> 00:50:58,096
Please connect me
to the governor-general's residence.

693
00:51:05,395 --> 00:51:06,646
Hello?

694
00:51:06,730 --> 00:51:07,689
Hello?

695
00:51:07,773 --> 00:51:10,025
This is the Government-General's
pneumatic tube room.

696
00:51:10,108 --> 00:51:12,611
We're sending a pneumatic tube carrier
to the governor-general.

697
00:51:12,694 --> 00:51:14,196
Make sure he receives it now.

698
00:51:16,865 --> 00:51:17,699
Sorry?

699
00:51:17,783 --> 00:51:19,868
It can't be delivered to His Excellency

700
00:51:19,951 --> 00:51:21,495
for another hour or so.

701
00:51:21,578 --> 00:51:23,580
He's taking a bath right now.

702
00:51:23,663 --> 00:51:25,499
He's taking a bath?

703
00:51:26,792 --> 00:51:28,251
Okay, understood.

704
00:51:30,504 --> 00:51:31,338
What do we do?

705
00:51:31,421 --> 00:51:34,257
Let's send it to
the inspector general's residence first.

706
00:51:37,594 --> 00:51:40,180
Operator, please put me through
to the inspector general's residence.

707
00:51:56,655 --> 00:51:57,739
<i>No one's answering.</i>

708
00:51:59,533 --> 00:52:01,201
No one's answering at the residence.

709
00:52:05,038 --> 00:52:07,040
Could you try one more time?

710
00:52:09,668 --> 00:52:10,752
Mr. Mitarai.

711
00:52:14,172 --> 00:52:15,340
Mr. Mitarai.

712
00:52:17,050 --> 00:52:18,051
Are you there?

713
00:52:25,183 --> 00:52:26,476
Ms. Keum. It's me.

714
00:52:27,978 --> 00:52:29,146
You're in there, aren't you?

715
00:52:30,230 --> 00:52:31,314
Come out right now.

716
00:52:31,398 --> 00:52:34,651
The police are looking everywhere
to arrest you.

717
00:52:34,734 --> 00:52:36,361
You have to run now.

718
00:52:37,028 --> 00:52:38,405
Is that Sato Hideo outside?

719
00:52:39,865 --> 00:52:41,616
Surely you're not falling for that?

720
00:52:43,076 --> 00:52:44,911
He's trying to arrest us.

721
00:52:49,291 --> 00:52:50,750
Let's send it anyway.

722
00:52:50,834 --> 00:52:51,918
What?

723
00:52:52,961 --> 00:52:54,337
INSPECTOR GENERAL

724
00:52:59,593 --> 00:53:01,094
I know you're in there.

725
00:53:02,387 --> 00:53:03,805
Please open the door.

726
00:53:03,889 --> 00:53:05,515
You have to trust me.

727
00:53:06,308 --> 00:53:07,142
Lee Ga-kyung!

728
00:53:09,811 --> 00:53:11,104
Get a hold of yourself.

729
00:53:15,942 --> 00:53:17,986
Put me through
to the inspector general's residence.

730
00:53:18,820 --> 00:53:20,071
I'm sorry, sir!

731
00:53:20,155 --> 00:53:22,032
There must have been some mistake!

732
00:53:22,115 --> 00:53:23,742
I'll go get her myself immediately!

733
00:53:36,046 --> 00:53:37,047
Yanagi.

734
00:53:40,258 --> 00:53:41,218
Yanagi!

735
00:53:52,729 --> 00:53:53,563
Hello?

736
00:53:54,189 --> 00:53:55,357
<i>Hello?</i>

737
00:53:58,109 --> 00:53:58,944
What's wrong?

738
00:54:00,445 --> 00:54:01,821
A little girl answered.

739
00:54:02,739 --> 00:54:03,949
I think she's Sato's daughter.

740
00:54:04,658 --> 00:54:05,492
What?

741
00:54:06,785 --> 00:54:09,287
I've got a little sister.
Her name is Hanako.

742
00:54:10,538 --> 00:54:11,539
<i>Hello?</i>

743
00:54:13,124 --> 00:54:14,376
Hello?

744
00:54:14,459 --> 00:54:15,460
Is this Hanako?

745
00:54:15,543 --> 00:54:16,711
What?

746
00:54:16,795 --> 00:54:19,089
How do you know my name?

747
00:54:19,172 --> 00:54:22,509
I'm a friend of your brother Hideo's.

748
00:54:22,592 --> 00:54:25,387
Hanako, are you in the study right now?

749
00:54:26,137 --> 00:54:28,139
Yes. Why?

750
00:54:29,140 --> 00:54:31,643
Could you put your father on the phone?

751
00:54:31,726 --> 00:54:33,144
I have an urgent matter to discuss.

752
00:54:33,728 --> 00:54:35,021
I can't.

753
00:54:35,105 --> 00:54:38,483
He's having dinner with guests right now.

754
00:54:38,566 --> 00:54:40,318
Okay, Hanako.

755
00:54:40,819 --> 00:54:43,363
Please get out of there right now.

756
00:54:43,947 --> 00:54:46,408
Wait, who are you?

757
00:54:47,033 --> 00:54:48,076
Are you…

758
00:54:49,077 --> 00:54:50,704
my brother's girlfriend?

759
00:54:51,371 --> 00:54:52,205
Well…

760
00:54:52,872 --> 00:54:53,748
Yes, I am.

761
00:54:53,832 --> 00:54:55,834
So come on, get out of there.

762
00:54:55,917 --> 00:54:56,751
You're lying.

763
00:54:56,835 --> 00:54:58,712
My brother doesn't have a girlfriend!

764
00:55:01,506 --> 00:55:02,340
Come on out.

765
00:55:03,425 --> 00:55:05,218
You need to run!

766
00:55:10,724 --> 00:55:11,558
Hanako.

767
00:55:13,226 --> 00:55:14,060
Wait.

768
00:55:14,144 --> 00:55:15,145
Something's arrived.

769
00:55:15,228 --> 00:55:18,023
Don't open that! Leave the room now!

770
00:55:18,106 --> 00:55:20,442
Why are you speaking to me informally?

771
00:55:21,693 --> 00:55:24,070
That thing is dangerous!

772
00:55:24,154 --> 00:55:26,156
Never, ever touch that.

773
00:55:26,239 --> 00:55:27,949
Get out of the study right now!

774
00:55:28,033 --> 00:55:29,701
Is it dangerous?

775
00:55:30,201 --> 00:55:31,119
How come?

776
00:55:31,202 --> 00:55:33,788
This came for my father.

777
00:55:34,748 --> 00:55:35,707
Please!

778
00:55:35,790 --> 00:55:38,209
You need to get out of there!

779
00:55:38,293 --> 00:55:40,170
Just leave it where it is!

780
00:55:44,257 --> 00:55:45,550
Here's white rice

781
00:55:46,217 --> 00:55:48,011
and <i>chutang </i>tofu soup.

782
00:55:54,559 --> 00:55:56,186
Who was that on the phone?

783
00:55:57,854 --> 00:55:59,272
Did someone call?

784
00:56:13,370 --> 00:56:14,704
Hanako!

785
00:56:14,788 --> 00:56:15,830
I'm begging you.

786
00:56:16,581 --> 00:56:18,625
Who are you, really?

787
00:56:18,708 --> 00:56:21,169
Are you really Hideo's girlfriend?

788
00:56:21,252 --> 00:56:24,547
No, that's not important right now.
Just hurry…

789
00:56:26,383 --> 00:56:27,300
Lee Ga-kyung!

790
00:56:28,051 --> 00:56:29,135
What are you doing?

791
00:56:31,930 --> 00:56:32,889
Lee Ga-kyung!

792
00:56:34,516 --> 00:56:35,600
Mr. Sato.

793
00:56:36,518 --> 00:56:39,020
You're not Hideo's girlfriend, are you?

794
00:56:42,524 --> 00:56:43,525
Hello?

795
00:56:44,192 --> 00:56:45,193
Hello?

796
00:56:48,655 --> 00:56:49,489
Hanako.

797
00:56:54,661 --> 00:56:55,829
Hanako!

798
00:57:01,501 --> 00:57:02,377
<i>Hanako.</i>

799
00:57:04,254 --> 00:57:05,213
Hideo?

800
00:57:05,296 --> 00:57:06,548
Hanako.

801
00:57:06,631 --> 00:57:08,133
Listen to me carefully.

802
00:57:08,216 --> 00:57:10,552
You have to get out
of the study now. Okay?

803
00:57:10,635 --> 00:57:12,804
Okay, I will.

804
00:57:19,227 --> 00:57:20,895
<i>By the way, Hideo.</i>

805
00:57:20,979 --> 00:57:23,189
<i>- That lady just now.</i>
- Hanako.

806
00:57:23,273 --> 00:57:25,275
- Is she really your girlfriend?
<i>- Hanako.</i>

807
00:57:25,358 --> 00:57:26,526
- She isn't, right?
<i>- Get out!</i>

808
00:57:26,609 --> 00:57:27,444
<i>- Hanako!</i>
<i>- </i>Hanako.

809
00:57:27,527 --> 00:57:28,862
<i>Hanako!</i>

810
00:57:28,945 --> 00:57:30,071
Who are you?

811
00:57:30,155 --> 00:57:31,114
So-ran.

812
00:57:49,090 --> 00:57:50,008
Hanako.

813
00:57:58,224 --> 00:57:59,601
Hanako. Hanako?

814
00:58:01,686 --> 00:58:02,520
Hanako.

815
00:58:03,646 --> 00:58:04,689
Hello?

816
00:58:06,441 --> 00:58:07,650
Hana… Hanako?

817
00:58:10,904 --> 00:58:11,946
Hanako!

818
00:59:20,431 --> 00:59:24,352
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

819
00:59:26,312 --> 00:59:28,314
Philip!

820
00:59:30,066 --> 00:59:32,443
Will you keep your mouth shut
like your husband did

821
00:59:32,527 --> 00:59:34,153
even if I shoot her dead?

822
00:59:36,573 --> 00:59:37,782
<i>Go ask them</i>

823
00:59:37,865 --> 00:59:40,159
<i>about my dead Joseon wife.</i>

824
00:59:40,702 --> 00:59:41,744
You have the same eyes.

825
00:59:42,328 --> 00:59:43,288
<i>Hideo.</i>

826
00:59:43,371 --> 00:59:45,540
What's making you so confused?

827
00:59:45,623 --> 00:59:46,708
Independence for Korea!

828
00:59:46,791 --> 00:59:48,126
Hideo!

829
00:59:58,428 --> 01:00:00,430
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
